WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.604
NVIDIA-based Linux AI systems commonly involve the NVIDIA driver,

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:06.719
CUDA-related runtime libraries, and sometimes a CUDA toolkit.

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:08.277
At a high level,

00:00:08.277 --> 00:00:12.560
the driver enables GPU operation and exposes capabilities to the system.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:18.401
The CUDA toolkit provides development tools and libraries used to build or run CUDA applications.

00:00:18.401 --> 00:00:22.295
These are related, but they are not the same thing.

00:00:22.295 --> 00:00:27.746
nvidia-smi is a common first check because it reports driver information, detected NVIDIA GPUs,

00:00:27.746 --> 00:00:31.640
utilization, memory use, temperature, power, and processes using the device.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.587
It is a useful signal,

00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:39.038
but it is not the final proof that a specific AI framework is working.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:44.489
A Python library, container, or inference runtime may still fail because of missing libraries,

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:46.826
incompatible versions, or incorrect environment configuration.

00:00:46.826 --> 00:00:47.994
Compatibility planning matters.

00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:51.888
Driver versions, CUDA runtime libraries, cuDNN and related acceleration libraries,

00:00:51.888 --> 00:00:56.171
Python packages, containers, and inference runtimes may all have version expectations.

00:00:56.171 --> 00:01:02.401
Randomly mixing versions can create errors that look like model failures but are really stack mismatches.

00:01:02.401 --> 00:01:08.242
Stable AI systems benefit from known-good combinations rather than constant chasing of the newest packages.

00:01:08.242 --> 00:01:13.304
GPU visibility should be checked from the places that matter: the host shell,

00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:16.029
Python environment, container, notebook, and inference server.

00:01:16.029 --> 00:01:19.534
Each layer can have different visibility and library paths.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:23.427
Document the driver version, runtime versions, container image, model runtime,

00:01:23.427 --> 00:01:24.596
and validation results.

00:01:24.596 --> 00:01:28.100
That documentation turns a working setup into something recoverable.
